          "commits": [
            {
              "message": "Merge remote-tracking branch 'upstream/main' into crop/esc-hides-frame\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcrates/ui-egui/src/tools/crop_ui.rs",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/photocraft/commit/f454c9622c96940f4ce658ba83918ee70da8766b",
              "date": "2026-11-04T03:04:20Z"
            },
            {
              "message": "format: bound blob inflation by the load's remaining budget; browser budgets (#10984)\n\nLoadFetch::blob_bounded decompressed a new blob up to max_blob_bytes\nand only then charged it against max_total_bytes. Successful blobs are\nretained, so several distinct, highly compressible blobs each allocated\na full max_blob_bytes before the total was checked. A new blob may now\ninflate only to what the total budget has left.\n\nThe browser build loaded native documents with the desktop defaults\n(1 GiB a blob, 16 GiB in all), far beyond a wasm32 instance's 4 GiB of\nlinear memory that the editor also uses. On wasm32 the defaults are now\n512 MiB a blob and 1 GiB in all.",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/photocraft/commit/37a01ca8746c121170644a07968d11263ef64407",
              "date": "2026-11-04T01:55:42Z"
            },
            {
              "message": "codecs: admit animated GIF screens, sparse RLE BMPs and icon PNG profiles (#10979)\n\n* codecs: admit animated GIF screens, sparse RLE BMPs and icon PNG profiles\n\n- Animated GIF decoding (decode_gif_frames) skipped the logical-screen\n  plausibility check the first-frame decode applies, although the\n  backend initializes the whole screen before reading a frame. Both now\n  share gif_plausible().\n- RLE BMPs skipped the file-size plausibility check entirely, so a\n  header-only file could make the decoder allocate and clear a\n  multi-gigabyte canvas. Like a GIF's screen, 256 MiB of canvas is now\n  free of data and the rest must be backed by the file.\n- The image crate's ICO decoder opens an embedded PNG with no limits,\n  and png inflates an iCCP profile while the decoder is built. Icon\n  PNG profiles are now inflated into a sink first and refused past\n  255 x 65519 bytes (or max_alloc), with a 64 MiB total across entries.\n\n* address review: visit each ICO profile chunk offset once",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/photocraft/commit/3225307e57802c76b540ee7a8691b5d635e447d8",
              "date": "2026-11-04T01:54:58Z"
            },
            {
              "message": "codecs: charge dropped PNG text against the metadata budget (#10980)\n\n* codecs: charge dropped PNG text against the metadata budget\n\nread_text_metadata debited the shared text allowance only for text it\nkept. A compressed iTXt chunk that inflated up to the whole remaining\nallowance and then failed UTF-8 validation (or hit a corrupt or\ntruncated stream) was dropped without being charged, so every further\nsuch chunk could repeat the same inflation. bounded_text now reports\nthe bytes it produced and the caller charges them whether or not the\ntext is kept.\n\n* codecs: charge the output a failing text decompress wrote\n\n* address review: charge Latin-1 zTXt error batch at UTF-8 length",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/photocraft/commit/d82e166494f95f9805af18d02e2121f29edd5ef5",
              "date": "2026-11-04T01:51:19Z"
            },
            {
              "message": "codecs: leave Extended XMP fragments out of zune-jpeg's header parse (#10981)\n\n* codecs: leave Extended XMP fragments out of zune-jpeg's header parse\n\nzune-jpeg 0.5 keeps every Extended XMP APP1 fragment until its GUID's\nset is complete, and re-sorts and re-checks the whole pending list\nafter every marker it parses. A file with many small, consistent but\nincomplete fragments (or a few followed by many other markers) costs\nquadratic time before any pixel is decoded.\n\nNothing in PhotoCraft reads zune's reassembled Extended XMP (metadata\ncomes from scan_metadata over the original bytes), so the decoder now\nhands zune a copy without those segments when a file has any. Files\nwithout Extended XMP are passed through unchanged.\n\n* codecs: reserve only the bytes kept after dropping Extended XMP segments",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/photocraft/commit/20f92ee405dc1c195a7a10ed54d2af9ca2ecef06",
              "date": "2026-11-04T01:50:58Z"
            }
          ]
